<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sudan becomes independent from Britain and Egypt</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>'s parliament ended the Anglo-Egyptian condominium and the country became a sovereign republic. It was among the first African states to gain independence after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-26">26 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nasser nationalises the Suez Canal</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gamal-abdel-nasser">Nasser</a> announced the nationalisation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> Company to fund the Aswan Dam. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and Israel invaded in October, but US pressure forced a humiliating withdrawal.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-9">9 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Elvis Presley first appears on The Ed Sullivan Show</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 60 million Americans, over 80 per cent of the TV audience, watched Elvis's first appearance on Sullivan's show. The 'waist up' camera shots came only on his third appearance in 1957.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-17">17 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Queen opens Calder Hall nuclear power station</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-ii">Elizabeth II</a> opened Calder Hall in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumberland">Cumberland</a>, the world's first nuclear power station to supply electricity to a national grid on a commercial scale. It also produced plutonium for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s weapons programme.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/budapest" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/budapest.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-23">23 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Hungarian Revolution begins in Budapest</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A student demonstration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> grew into a national uprising against the communist government and Soviet control. Soviet forces crushed it in November, leaving some 2,500 Hungarians dead and 200,000 in exile.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-31">31 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Britain and France begin bombing Egypt over Suez</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British and French aircraft attacked Egyptian airfields after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> rejected their ultimatum to withdraw from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suez-canal">Suez Canal</a> zone. US and Soviet pressure forced a humiliating withdrawal.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/budapest" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/budapest.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-4">4 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet tanks move in to crush the Hungarian Revolution</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces launched a massive assault on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a> at dawn, overthrowing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imre-nagy">Imre Nagy</a>'s government. Thousands were killed, and the West did not intervene.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/suez-crisis" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suez-crisis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis · War</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/suez-crisis">Suez Crisis</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Suez Crisis was the international crisis of 1956 in which Britain, France and Israel invaded Egypt after Gamal Abdel Nasser nationalised the Suez Canal.</p></div></li></ol></section>
